>> title: Cubiletes de Queso
>> category: Custards & Puddings
>> tags: cheese, pastry, mexican, baked, make-ahead
>> counters: Panadería
>> aka: cubilete, cubiletes, cubilete de queso, cheese cup, mexican cheese tart, pastel de queso, queso cup
>> pairs-with: queso-fresco
>> servings: 12
>> time: 3 hr 30 min
>> slack: narrow — the filling is set at twenty-five minutes with a wobble still on it; one taken firm in the oven cracks and weeps as it cools

>> step: rub the butter into the dry
Rub @cold unsalted butter{1/2%cup}(115 g) into @all-purpose flour{1 1/2%cup}(180 g) and @powdered sugar{1/4%cup}(30 g) to coarse crumbs.

>> step: bring together, chill 30 min
Bring @&(~1)crumbs{} together with @egg yolk{1}(18 g) and @cold water{1%Tbs}(15 mL), then ~chill{30%min}.

>> step: press into 12 cups
Press @&(~1)pastry{} thin into 12 cups of a muffin #tin{}, up the sides to the rim, and prick the bases.

>> step: beat the filling smooth
Beat @cream cheese{8%oz}(225 g), @crumbled queso fresco{4%oz}(115 g), @granulated sugar{1/2%cup}(100 g), @eggs{2%large}(100 g), @vanilla extract{1%tsp}(5 mL) and @lime zest{1%tsp} smooth.

>> step: fill and bake at 350°F 25 min
Spoon @&(~1)cheese filling{} into @&(~2)lined cups{} to just under the rim and bake at 350°F for ~bake{25%min}, until the edges are set and the centres still wobble.

>> step: cool, then chill 2 hr
Cool @&(~1)baked cubiletes{} in the tin ~cool{30%min}, then ~chill{2%hr} before lifting them out.
